1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,953
A Moon base may breathe 30% oxygen at 10.2 psi. Does NASA’s fire data cover it?

2
00:00:03,003 --> 00:00:06,513
EMBER ranks 20 NASA combustion investigations against your habitat

3
00:00:06,563 --> 00:00:09,781
Key finding: no solid-material test in NASA’s data goes above 22.2% oxygen

4
00:00:09,831 --> 00:00:12,742
Every NASA test row is one click from a modeller’s CSV

5
00:00:12,792 --> 00:00:17,832
Gemini writes the analysis. EMBER rejects any quote or number not found in the sources it cites

6
00:00:17,882 --> 00:00:21,594
It shows what the research informs: detection, suppression, ventilation

7
00:00:21,644 --> 00:00:24,655
…and where it helps on Earth: mines, aircraft, submarines

8
00:00:24,705 --> 00:00:27,066
Open NASA data, checked AI, honest limits
